Yes — if you mean **MCP = Model Context Protocol**, there are several MCP servers for carbon / emissions data. The right one depends on what kind of emissions data you need:

| Use case | MCP option | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Company emissions / corporate carbon footprints** | **Mycelium emissions database** | Live, read-only MCP server for company emissions; no API key or sign-up required. It says data is tagged as company-reported or Mycelium-estimated. ([mycelium.global](https://mycelium.global/mcp)) |
| **US grid / Scope 2 electricity emissions by ZIP code** | **emission-factors MCP server** | No API key; covers EPA eGRID, EIA rates, hourly grid carbon intensity, EPA CAMD plant emissions, utility tariffs; includes tools like `calculate_emissions`, `hourly_intensity`, and `plant_emissions`. ([github.com](https://github.com/rozetyp/emission-factors-mcp)) |
| **General emissions calculations / factors** | **Climatiq MCP Server** | Community MCP server for the Climatiq API; supports electricity, travel, freight, procurement, cloud-computing, hotels, custom emission factors, etc.; requires a Climatiq API key. ([github.com](https://github.com/jagan-shanmugam/climatiq-mcp-server)) |
| **Citable emission factors / provenance-heavy factor lookup** | **GreenCalculus MCP** | Designed to return emission factors with publisher/source reference, data version, and proof link; searching factors can work without a key, while calculations/full lookups need a key. ([greencalculus.com](https://greencalculus.com/developers/agents/)) |
| **Flight emissions** | **Google Travel Impact Model MCP** | Official Google MCP endpoint for flight emissions; supports specific upcoming flights, typical airport-pair emissions, and historical Scope 3 flight emissions; requires a Google Cloud API key. ([developers.google.com](https://developers.google.com/travel/impact-model/docs/mcp)) |
| **Broader Scope 1/2/3 workflows** | **`sankalpsthakur/carbon`** | Open-source AI agent + MCP toolkit with 6 MCP servers and tools for Scope 1/2/3 carbon accounting and decarbonization workflows. ([github.com](https://github.com/sankalpsthakur/carbon)) |
| **Carbon estimation APIs for business workflows** | **CarbonSutra MCP** | Vendor MCP server for carbon estimation use cases across flights, hotels, ecommerce, freight, vehicles, fuel, electricity, and ESG workflows. ([carbonsutra.com](https://www.carbonsutra.com/mcp-server)) |

A couple of quick examples:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "mycelium": {
      "url": "https://mycelium.global/mcp/server"
    }
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "emission-factors": {
      "url": "https://emission-factors.com/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

One caveat: there is also a product named **Carbon** with an MCP server, but it appears to be for **manufacturing/ERP data**, not carbon-emissions datasets. ([docs.carbon.ms](https://docs.carbon.ms/mcp))
